note over McpClient
Module-level helpers:
  get_client() — creates MultiServerMCPClient pointing to settings.mcp_server_url
  get_db_uri() — builds PostgreSQL URI from settings fields with quote_plus password encoding
  get_pii_middleware() — returns 3 PIIMiddleware instances (email redact, credit_card mask, phone redact)
  get_summarization_middleware() — builds SummarizationMiddleware with dedicated summary LLM
  get_hitl_middleware() — returns HumanInTheLoopMiddleware configured for add_order approval only;
    check_menu and check_order_status are False (auto-approved, no interrupt)
  load_session_context(session) — loads tools + system prompt + all resources unconditionally,
    returns (tools, system_text) ready for agent creation
  extract_pending_approval(result) — inspects result["__interrupt__"] and returns
    {tool, args, description} if a HITL interrupt is pending, or None if agent completed
  resume_agent(decision, thread_id) — rebuilds agent with same middleware and checkpointer,
    then calls ainvoke(Command(resume={"decisions": [{"type": decision}]})) to continue
    from the saved interrupt point in the checkpointer
  has_pending_interrupt(thread_id)
    checks if result["__interrupt__"] is present

All resources (menu://items, store://info) are always loaded unconditionally.
No intent detection or resource filtering.

